# Unambiguous names

A basename must identify the concept **without opening the file**. Applies to
`src/`, `tests/`, `docs/`, `.cursor/`, and packages — not only tests.

## Rules

- Prefer the **domain term** over a short generic noun (`judgement_policy`, not `policy`).
- Mirror source ↔ test: `foo.py` ↔ `test_foo.py` (or language equivalent).
- One concern per test module — no bag files (`test_misc.py`).
- If two peers could share a short name, pick the longer disambiguator at the leaf.
- When renaming public imports, prefer a thin re-export shim and update call sites/docs in the same change when practical.

## Litmus

From a directory listing, would a newcomer pick the right file for the concept
they have in mind? If not, rename before merge.

```text
# BAD
policy.py / test_policy.py / test_phases.py

# GOOD
judgement_policy.py / test_judgement_policy.py
test_graph.py, test_routing.py, …
```
